A||N||1||turbo86se||Awesome bogey on 12th hole!||||7||
Z||000000||turbo86se||08-15-2000||12:23 AM||||I can't believe it! Today I was hitting some balls at Indigo Creek, feeling out my new 5-wood and trying to get out this slump with my irons. Well, I got a quick lesson from the assistant pro Rob, turned out I was moving my lower body on my backswing, and moving my head up. Got that straightened out and started hitting my irons great! After a couple bags of balls, I get set up ready to play 18. The front nine was ok, but when I made the turn I caught up with a foursome. I was playing solo, so I had to wait a while to tee off. This is when it gets good. The 12th hole is a 355 yard par 4, dogleg left, with a stream that comes into play twice. I teed up with my new 5-wood, and cranked it about 180-190 yards, down the center of the fairway! The foursome on the upper part of the fairway notices my shot, and signals me to play through. Now I'm nervous. I'm not a great golfer, I do hit some good shots, and I haven't broke 100 consistantly, yet. My second shot would have a perfect lye to the green, if not for the huge tree about 30 yards in front of me in the center of the fairway. The foursome is looking at me and waiting on my shot, the pressure is on! I drop my 7 wood and pick up my 7 iron. I tried to remember everything Rob said, nice easy backswing, eye on the ball, follow through high. I hit the ball really good, it went high and right of the tree, it did catch a branch, resting short but over the stream, luckily. I might have hit the 7 iron 80 yards b/c of the tree. I get up to my ball, about 80 yards to the pin. Everyone is still looking at me, and I hit my sandwedge left, in the fringe off the green. Whew! The worst part is over. Grab my 8 iron and putter to my fourth shot. Everyone is still looking at me, I chipped the ball about 20 yards, to about 3 feet past the hole, got some compliments there!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>Now I'm putting three feet for bogey. I look at the line from every angle, practice swing, concentrate on that line on the sweet spot on the putter, and sink the ball in the cup!! YEAH!! I was so thrilled! Got some more compliments! I couldn't believe it! I thought I was going to really embarrass myself! The rest of the back nine was good, kept crushing my 5 wood at the tee, but nothing made me feel as good as making those shots in front of people you know are watching you.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>I'm so proud of myself!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><BR> ||||reg||7
Z||000001||zeusrekning||08-15-2000||08:01 PM||||congratulations joel!<BR>Have no idea what you are talking about though. I have kinda wanted to learn to play golf but,,, don't really think i got the time. how's the fiero family&gt;?||||reg||1
